; The edge cases of the operators SMT-LIB's FixedSizeBitVectors fixes and BTOR2 inherits, applied to
; inputs rather than constants, so that no constant folding answers them: division and remainder
; by zero and with every sign, shifts past the width, rotation by more than the width, the
; overflow predicates at their boundaries, and widths 1 and 3. Each block is "x = c1 /\ y = c2 /\
; op(x, y) != want"; the bad property is their disjunction, so the model is safe iff every
; operator gives its expected value.
1 sort bitvec 8
2 sort bitvec 1
3 sort bitvec 3
4 input 1 x
5 input 1 y
6 input 3 x3
7 input 3 y3
8 input 2 x1
9 input 2 y1
